import json
D=[]
def a(i,d,q,r,c=None):
    o={"item_id":i,"decision":d,"quote":q,"reason":r}
    if c: o["corrected"]=c
    D.append(o)
a("D016","CONTESTED","6/16/23: Engineer talked with design engineering to understand the history of the parts involved.","A conversation with design engineering is both a meeting (OTHER) and an inquiry conducted to find the cause (INVESTIGATION_START); the rules do not settle which.")
a("D017","CONTESTED","6/17/23: Engineer visited manufacturing to understand the process of installation. Engineer received plant process document.","The versions label different sentences of the 6/17 entry. Each is defensible: receiving a document is OTHER, and the visit to understand installation is plausibly INVESTIGATION_START. Because the pairing is misaligned, neither can be chosen over the other.")
a("D018","Y","6/26/23: Warranty search completed. Found 7 warranty claims stating checked U-bolt hitting the fuel tank.","Y types the warranty search as INVESTIGATION_START, an analysis conducted to find the scope, which is correct. X types the warranty-claim finding as OTHER, but warranty claims reaching the filer are FILER_AWARENESS.")
a("D019","Y","Found 7 warranty claims stating checked U-bolt hitting the fuel tank.","Warranty claims found by the filer are a report of the problem reaching it, so FILER_AWARENESS is right. X's OTHER label for 'Reassembled and checked clearances' is a different sentence and does not address this event's type.")
a("D020","X","7/13/23: Reached out to PTC about testing and communicated the dynamic gap study requested","This is a communication to arrange testing that had already been requested on 7/11. It does not open the testing itself (parts only arrived on 7/25), so OTHER.")
a("D021","X","8/22/23: Initial test was completed, and the data was collected.","Completing a test and collecting its data is a test result or occurrence, which is OTHER. It does not open or start an investigation.")
a("D022","Y","9/1/23: Population was scanned for errors.","Scanning the population is an analysis conducted to find the scope, so INVESTIGATION_START.")
a("D023","Y","9/1/23: Population was scanned for errors. No errors found. Final Warranty Search","'Final Warranty Search' is a search conducted to find the scope, so INVESTIGATION_START (consistent with the 6/26 warranty search). 'No errors found' is a negative status or result with no action, not a separate event.")
a("D024","X","Reassembled and checked clearances. No further issues were found.","'No further issues were found' is a negative status statement with no action (like 'no reports of ...'), so it is not an event.")
a("D025","Y","6/27/23: Presented investigation to safety committee. Needed further information to make decision.","'Needed further information to make decision' states a need or status and reports no action, so it is not an event.")
a("D026","NEITHER","9/1/23: Population was scanned for errors. No errors found. Final Warranty Search","The 'Final Warranty Search' event exists (Y has it, matched in D023), but as a warranty search conducted to find the scope it is INVESTIGATION_START, not OTHER.",{"date_text":"9/1/23","type":"INVESTIGATION_START","quote":"Final Warranty Search","inherited_date":True,"entry_quote":"9/1/23: Population was scanned for errors.","date_inferred":False})
a("D027","Y","June 5, 2023, during an internal audit, it was determined that a steering column pinch bolt was not properly secured, and an internal investigation was initiated.","The rules list an internal audit finding explicitly under FILER_AWARENESS, and it is the sentence's main clause. Opening the investigation is secondary to it. One event per sentence.")
a("D028","X","June 27, 2023, through August 31, 2023, Autocar inspected 176 additional units and zero defects were found.","The sentence has two distinct dates bounding an activity, not a production data window, so the rules give one event per date. The August 31 event exists, and inspecting units to find the scope is INVESTIGATION_START.")
a("D029","X","September 18, 2023  Volvo Product Safety Office receives a report of a potential issue in our factory with a critical joint and a formal investigation is opened.","The main clause is that the filer receives a report of the issue, which is FILER_AWARENESS. One event per sentence. Opening the investigation follows from that report.")
a("D030","X","PSRI 23-069 Castle Nut Under-torqued.","This is a reference title or label with no action or occurrence, so it is not an event.")
a("D031","Y","September 12, 2023, during an internal inspection, Autocar personnel identified three units equipped with the suspect pressure switch, not included in recall 23V400 suspect population and began investigation.","An internal inspection finding of the issue is FILER_AWARENESS (internal audit finding). It is the primary clause, and beginning the investigation is secondary. One event per sentence.")
a("D032","Y","On August 1, 2023, a Lucid Air customer experienced charring of a rear seat.","The sentence reports the field incident itself, not a report or notice reaching Lucid, so it is OTHER (an occurrence).")
a("D033","X","Lucid Engineering briefed Lucid’s Product Safety Working Group (PSWG) about the issue on August 3, after which, Engineering continued its analysis of the risk of harm from the issue.","An internal briefing between Lucid groups is a meeting, which is OTHER. It is not a report reaching the filer from outside, because Lucid already knew of the issue.")
a("D034","Y","Lucid released the Remedy S/W Version for customer vehicles to download starting on October 10.","Releasing the remedy software for owners' vehicles is remedy logistics (repair of the affected vehicles), so it is not an event.")
a("D035","X","As of October 4, Affected S/W Versions are no longer being installed on or transmitted to any vehicles.","An 'As of <date>' status statement is excluded from events.")
a("D036","CONTESTED","From October 2022, through January 2023, FCA US TSRC analyzed warranty claims, customer records, and vehicle history to identify incidents of third-row seat belt buckles being damaged during assembly. In parallel,","The versions label different sentences. Each is correct for its own sentence: the warranty analysis is INVESTIGATION_START, and the meetings sentence that inherits October 2022 from the bullet is OTHER. Because the pairing is misaligned, neither can be chosen.")
a("D037","CONTESTED","From June 2023, through September 2023, FCA US TSRC finalized discussions with FCA US Restraints Engineering, Interior Engineering, and Manufacturing and determined the suspect population.","The versions label different events. X's September 2023 end date of the June-September range is a valid OTHER event. Y's September 27 recognition is a valid FILER_AWARENESS event. Because the pairing is misaligned, neither can be chosen.")
a("D038","X","From October 2022, through January 2023, FCA US TSRC analyzed warranty claims, customer records, and vehicle history to identify incidents of third-row seat belt buckles being damaged during assembly.","The sentence has two distinct dates bounding an activity (not a production window), so there is one event per date. The January 2023 event exists, and the analysis is INVESTIGATION_START.")
a("D039","Y","From June 2023, through September 2023, FCA US TSRC finalized discussions with FCA US Restraints Engineering, Interior Engineering, and Manufacturing and determined the suspect population.","There is one event per distinct date. The June 2023 start of this activity is an event, and finalizing discussions and determining the population is OTHER.")
a("D040","NEITHER","On September 27, 2023, the FCA US TSRC organization recognized a vehicle build issue existed on certain vehicles related to third-row seat belt buckles being inaccessible or damaged, potentially resulting in a noncompliance","The September 27 event exists, but the filer recognizing that the issue exists is FILER_AWARENESS, not OTHER. It is not yet a DECISION, because it says 'potentially' and the recall decision came on October 19.",{"date_text":"September 27, 2023","type":"FILER_AWARENESS","quote":"On September 27, 2023, the FCA US TSRC organization recognized a vehicle build issue existed on certain vehicles related to third-row seat belt buckles being inaccessible or damaged, potentially resulting in a noncompliance with FMVSS No. 208 Occupant Crash Protection","inherited_date":False,"date_inferred":False})
json.dump(D,open("decisions.json","w"),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)
